From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] sagit: stop clang from emitting LSE/RCPC atomics

Kryo 280 is an ARMv8.0 core without the LSE or RCPC extensions, but the
Darwin arm64 target defaults enable both regardless of -march, so ordinary
os_atomic operations were lowered to ldadd/stadd and acquire loads to
ldapr.  On hardware the first of those trapped with an undefined
instruction at lck_grp_reference+0x8 (ldadd w8, w8, [x1]).

Negate the features explicitly; -march=armv8-a+nolse is not enough because
the Darwin CPU default re-enables it afterwards.  SWEET (ARMv8.2) keeps
LSE and is unaffected.
---
 makedefs/MakeInc.def | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/makedefs/MakeInc.def b/makedefs/MakeInc.def
--- a/makedefs/MakeInc.def
+++ b/makedefs/MakeInc.def
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_VMAPPLE = -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_VMAPPLE              -march=armv8.5a
 MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_BCM2837 = -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_BCM2837
 MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_SWEET = -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET                -march=armv8.2-a+crypto
-MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_SAGIT = -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SAGIT -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET -march=armv8-a+crypto
+MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_SAGIT = -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SAGIT -DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET -march=armv8-a+crypto -Xclang -target-feature -Xclang -lse -Xclang -target-feature -Xclang -rcpc
 
 
 #
